picotool for Debian
====================

picotool's build (CMakeLists.txt) requires PICO_SDK_PATH to point at a
checkout of https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk, version 2.1.0 or later.
It is only used for headers and version metadata by default (USE_PRECOMPILED
is on, so the pre-built enc_bootloader.elf / xip_ram_perms.elf checked into
this source tree are reused instead of being recompiled), so no
arm-none-eabi toolchain is needed to build this package.

Before running dpkg-buildpackage, export PICO_SDK_PATH:

    export PICO_SDK_PATH=/path/to/pico-sdk
    dpkg-buildpackage -b -uc -us

debian/rules picks it up from the environment; the build aborts with a clear
error if it is unset.

This packaging deliberately diverges from the picotool package in the
Debian archive proper, which build-depends on the pico-sdk-source package
and rebuilds enc_bootloader/xip_ram_perms from source with USE_PRECOMPILED=0.
That approach requires the arm-none-eabi cross toolchain and the mbedtls
submodule; this simplified packaging avoids both for local/personal builds.
